285	
286	## `set_video`
287	
288	Merges a patch into each clip's own video properties, as one undo step however many clips it names. It mirrors the Clip tab's [Picture sub-tab](/canvas/picture-tab/) and [Color sub-tab](/color/color-tab/).
289	
290	| Argument | Type | Required | What it does |
291	| --- | --- | --- | --- |
292	| `clips` | array of integers | Yes | The clips to change, at least one. `get_project` lists their ids. |
293	| `patch` | object | Yes | The properties to change. The rest of this page lists its keys. |
294	| `scope` | integer | No | A nest id, to edit inside that nest. See [Editing inside a nest](/mcp/nests/). |
295	| `project` | string | No | The path of the open project to act on, as `get_project` reports it. Leave it out for the frontmost one. |
296	
297	```json
298	{ "clips": [12, 14], "patch": { "opacity": 0.8, "shadow": { "blur": 20 } } }
299	```
300	
301	**How a patch merges.** A key you leave out keeps its value, inside a nested object too, so `{shadow: {blur: 20}}` keeps the shadow's colour, angle and distance. On a clip that has no shadow yet, the keys you left out take the defaults listed below. `shadow`, `chroma`, `reflection`, `spotlight`, `motion`, `look`, `cursor`, `cutout` and `hide_silent` set to `null` clear that property. `filters` and `obscure` are lists, so each replaces whole: send the full list, or `[]` to clear it. See [Patches](/mcp/patches/).
302	
303	**Colours.** A colour is four numbers, `[r, g, b, a]`, each 0 to 1. Three numbers are refused, and so is a value outside the range. The chroma key's colour is the one exception: three numbers, with no alpha.
304	
305	**What it answers.** The usual edit answer: `ok` and the `project` summary. If the patch changes nothing, the call says so and leaves no undo step. See [What a call answers](/mcp/what-a-call-answers/).
306	
307	**When it refuses.**
308	
309	- A key or value the patch doesn't know is an error naming its dotted path, array indices included, and the value you sent, such as `filters[1].kind`. Nothing is dropped, corrected or clamped.
310	- A number outside its range is an error naming the key, the range and the number.
311	- A clip with no video properties is an error: "clip 7 has no video properties".
312	- The sections below list what a particular kind of clip can't take.
313	
314	### Which key does what
315	
316	| Keys | Section |
317	| --- | --- |
318	| `x`, `y`, `scale`, `rotation`, `opacity`, `blend` | [Transform](#transform-position-scale-rotation-opacity-and-blend) |
319	| `crop`, `corner_radius` | [Crop and corners](#crop-and-corners) |
320	| `shadow`, `chroma`, `filters`, `reflection`, `spotlight`, `obscure` | [Effects](#effects-shadow-chroma-key-filters-reflection-spotlight-and-obscure) |
321	| `cutout` | [Remove Background](#cutout) |
322	| `behind_subject` | [Text Behind Subject](#behind_subject) |
323	| `cursor` | [The recorded cursor](#cursor) |
324	| `motion` | [Motion presets](#motion) |
325	| `motion_blur` | [Motion blur](#motion_blur) |
326	| `hide_silent` | [Hide While Silent](#hide_silent) |
327	| `color`, `wheels`, `curves`, `look`, `qualifier` | [Light and colour](#color), [wheels](#wheels), [curves](#curves), [looks and LUTs](#look), [the qualifier](#qualifier) |
328	
329	### On an adjustment clip
330	
331	An [adjustment clip](/color/adjustment-clips/) has no picture of its own. Only `color`, `wheels`, `curves`, `look`, the sepia, noir, vignette and invert filters, and `opacity` (the grade's strength) do anything there, and `qualifier` narrows which pixels they reach. The blur, sharpen and pixelate filters and any blend mode are errors, such as "clip 7 is an adjustment clip and cannot take the blur filter".
